<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-NAB says Rayner to be new chairman.</title>
<headline>RTRS-NAB says Rayner to be new chairman.</headline>
<dateline>MELBOURNE 1996-01-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>National Australia Bank (NAB) said on Thursday its chairman William Irvine would retire from the board in September 1997.</p>
<p>Irvine said in a statement Mark Rayner, a director, would succeed him.</p>
<p>Irvine, 68, was appointed chairman in 1992 and has been a director since 1979. Rayner is also chairman of Pasminco Ltd and deputy of Comalco Ltd.</p>
<p>-- Melbourne Bureau 61-3 9286-1421</p>
</text>
